<https://blueprinting.dlab5.net/i/patterns/Constraint/constraint-generated-artefacts-committed> a archimate:Constraint;
    archimate:identifier "constraint-generated-artefacts-committed";
    archimate:name "Generated artefacts are committed";
    archimate:documentation "The deployment pipeline then needs no ontology toolchain and cannot drift because upstream moved. The cost is that regeneration must be verified in CI, or the source and the output diverge silently.";
    archimate:hasProperty _:p-e-constraint-generated-artefacts-committed-0.
_:p-e-constraint-generated-artefacts-committed-0 a archimate:Property;
    archimate:propertyKey "reference";
    archimate:propertyValue "docs/adr/0004-metamodel-generated-from-the-ontology.md".
<https://blueprinting.dlab5.net/i/patterns/Constraint/constraint-illegal-connections-unofferable> a archimate:Constraint;
    archimate:identifier "constraint-illegal-connections-unofferable";
    archimate:name "An illegal connection must be unofferable, not merely rejected";
    archimate:documentation "Typed variable references, with variableTypes taken from the metamodel's own relationship matrix. A validator that complains afterwards teaches a user that the tool is annoying; a palette that cannot express the mistake teaches them the language.";
    archimate:hasProperty _:p-e-constraint-illegal-connections-unofferable-0.
_:p-e-constraint-illegal-connections-unofferable-0 a archimate:Property;
    archimate:propertyKey "reference";
    archimate:propertyValue "packages/blockly/src/generate.ts".
<https://blueprinting.dlab5.net/i/patterns/Constraint/constraint-overlay-declares-conventions> a archimate:Constraint;
    archimate:identifier "constraint-overlay-declares-conventions";
    archimate:name "Application conventions live in an overlay, as annotation properties";
    archimate:documentation "Declared as owl:AnnotationProperty with sh:in for enumerations and sh:defaultValue for defaults, so a convention is data the generator reads rather than a constant in application code. Adding a value is an ontology change, not a code change.";
    archimate:hasProperty _:p-e-constraint-overlay-declares-conventions-0.
_:p-e-constraint-overlay-declares-conventions-0 a archimate:Property;
    archimate:propertyKey "reference";
    archimate:propertyValue "ontology/overlay/blueprinting-app-metadata.ttl; digitalhome-cloud-core schema/tbox/dhc-app-metadata.ttl".
<https://blueprinting.dlab5.net/i/patterns/Constraint/constraint-pipeline-deploy-in-a-subshell> a archimate:Constraint;
    archimate:identifier "constraint-pipeline-deploy-in-a-subshell";
    archimate:name "pipeline-deploy runs in a subshell";
    archimate:documentation "Amplify runs every command in one persistent shell, so a bare `cd backend` leaks into the frontend phase and its npm ci then runs against the wrong lockfile. The symptom names a package the root lockfile does not contain, so it reads as a dependency problem rather than a directory one.";
    archimate:hasProperty _:p-e-constraint-pipeline-deploy-in-a-subshell-0.
_:p-e-constraint-pipeline-deploy-in-a-subshell-0 a archimate:Property;
    archimate:propertyKey "instances";
    archimate:propertyValue "blueprinting-dlab5-net".
